  "notes": "One form for procedures, functions and scheduled events (merged 2026-11-05: the descriptor service serves one form per family, so the separate function and event forms were never served); the variant comes from the kind. Routines: create binds the native routine compiler with its review (SQL mode identity and MySQL Shell 9.7 grammar); editing binds ALTER PROCEDURE/FUNCTION, which changes only the comment, SQL security and data access, so the body, parameters, return type, determinism, language and definer show locked on reopen and the characteristics pre-fill with their current values. Events: create and ALTER EVENT with every option; omitted options stay unchanged, and the schedule pre-fills from SHOW CREATE EVENT. Round-tripped 2026-11-05 on the MySQL 9.7.0 demo (tools/tests/test_ui_descriptor_roundtrip_mysql.py)."
